What a content rule list blocked, told to the application through the C
API (Kosmos docs/adblock.md, step B1). WebKit's web process tells the UI
process of every request a list blocked and every load whose cookies it
kept back, but the C API's navigation client passes on only `notify`
rules' names, so a C application cannot count what was kept out. On
Kosmos those two are passed on as well, under names no rule can give
itself: `kosmos:blocked` and `kosmos:cookies`. JetSki's shield counts them.

diff -ruN a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/API/C/WKPage.cpp b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/API/C/WKPage.cpp
--- a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/API/C/WKPage.cpp	2026-11-16 08:03:07.195449598 -0300
+++ b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/API/C/WKPage.cpp	2026-11-16 08:03:07.211952123 -0300
@@ -2515,6 +2515,19 @@
                     apiListIdentifiers.append(API::String::create(listIdentifier));
                     apiNotifications.append(API::String::create(notification));
                 }
+#if OS(KOSMOS)
+                // Kosmos: what a list blocked is said too, as two names no
+                // `notify` rule can have - Privacy and Ad Blocking counts
+                // them on JetSki's shield (Kosmos docs/adblock.md).
+                if (result.blockedLoad) {
+                    apiListIdentifiers.append(API::String::create(listIdentifier));
